<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5353" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bīmātus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		bimus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the age of two years</i> (of animals and plants): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ante bimatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 5, 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 3, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 4, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(polypi) ultra bimatum non vivunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 30, 48, § 89</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 21, 24,
				§ 73</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neque his bimatu longior vita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					30, 48, § 93</span></i>
			.—Of children, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt. 2</span></i>;
		<i><span class="en">16</span></i>.</div>
